                <pb facs="0543" n="1277" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1277"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 19.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 615.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith for
                    your information copy of a dispatch from Consul Gibson to Consul-General Short,
                    with copy of Dr. Christie’s report and translated copy of the report of the
                    moutessarif of Mersine, all relating to the Tarsus affair.</p>
                <p>In this connection, I would call the attention of the Department to the
                    gratifying fact that the grand vizier has kept the promise he made me on August
                    7, viz, that he would take prompt action in the matter. This action, looking to
                    the protection of the Americans in Tarsus and the arrest of the guilty parties,
                    seems to have been taken some days before the receipt, in America, of the
                    telegrams which so greatly excited our Christian press. I shall now spare no
                    efforts at the Porte to secure the punishment of the guilty parties.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>





